    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d851">

                <pb facs="0923" n="913" xml:id="pg913"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.8890/3–1449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-14T19:00:00+08:00">March 14, 1949—7
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 14—6:27 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>875. Jardine-Matheson<anchor n="93" xml:id="d851-f1"/> Shanghai received telegram
                    March 11 from Tientsin agents not to despatch any steamers Taku Bar pending
                    issuance new Communist shipping regulations due shortly. Their steamer had
                    already left Hong Kong with Tientsin cargo aboard so was diverted Pusan. Will
                    proceed Tientsin later, if possible. However, Butterfield and Swire Steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hanyang</hi> also with Hong Kong cargo expected arrive
                    Taku about March 15. Butterfield and Swire state they have no previous Communist
                    clearance but are hopeful discharge possible. American President Line will not
                    send in another ship until Tientsin agent assures them arrangements load outward
                    cargo completed.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 875, repeated Nanking 520, Canton 156.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d851-f1" n="93" xml:id="d851-f1-content">
                <p>British shipping firm.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
